{"additional":"","additionalPlain":"","categories":{"commitment":"Freelance","department":"Welo Data - AI Services","location":"Japan","team":"AI Service General Application","allLocations":["Japan"]},"createdAt":1785392684324,"descriptionPlain":"We’re seeking an experienced Quality Reviewer to audit work completed by raters evaluating a personalization feature within a maps/search experience.\nAs a Reviewer, you will ensure outputs meet formatting and guideline requirements, are logically aligned to scenarios, and include complete, accurate evidence. \n \nContract type: Freelance\nLanguage: Japanese (Japan)\nEstimated volume: Approximately 30 hours per week, depending on the required review target and project volume. \nStart date: ASAP\n \nWhat you will do:\nReview rater worksheets for compliance with formatting requirements.\nVerify that responses are logically correct and aligned with the assigned scenarios.\nAssess ratings and rationales for accuracy, consistency, and completeness.\nConfirm that required screenshots, retrievals, and personalization evidence meet project guidelines.\nProvide clear, concise, and actionable feedback; request corrections where needed.\nFlag ambiguous cases, systemic issues, or guideline gaps to the project team.\n","description":"<div>\n<div>We’re seeking an experienced Quality Reviewer to audit work completed by raters evaluating a personalization feature within a maps/search experience.</div>\n<div>As a Reviewer, you will ensure outputs meet formatting and guideline requirements, are logically aligned to scenarios, and include complete, accurate evidence.&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Contract type:</strong> Freelance</div>\n<div><strong>Language:</strong> Japanese (Japan)</div>\n<div><strong>Estimated volume: </strong><span data-teams=\"true\">Approximately 30 hours per week, depending on the required review target and project volume.</span>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</div>\n</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>What you will do:</strong></div>\n<div>\n<ul>\n<li>Review rater worksheets for compliance with formatting requirements.</li>\n<li>Verify that responses are logically correct and aligned with the assigned scenarios.</li>\n<li>Assess ratings and rationales for accuracy, consistency, and completeness.</li>\n<li>Confirm that required screenshots, retrievals, and personalization evidence meet project guidelines.</li>\n<li>Provide clear, concise, and actionable feedback; request corrections where needed.</li>\n<li>Flag ambiguous cases, systemic issues, or guideline gaps to the project team.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","id":"2e0cf51e-414f-409d-95e0-526c7079e26e","lists":[{"text":"Requirements:  ","content":"\n<li>To be located and have the right to work in Japan.</li>\n<li>An existing, actively used <strong>Gmail account</strong></li>\n<li>Proven experience in Quality Audit/QA review (content evaluation, relevance, or similar).</li>\n<li>Familiarity with maps/local search user experiences and personalization concepts.</li>\n<li>Strong proficiency with spreadsheets (Google Sheets or equivalent).</li>\n<li>Excellent attention to detail and consistent application of guidelines.</li>\n<li>Clear written communication and a constructive feedback style.</li>\n\n<div><em>Please note: </em></div>\n\n<li><em>This project requires opt-in, consent-based access to limited elements of your activity history. A consent form will be provided for you to review and sign before participation. Please note that the consent form and its terms may be subject to change as project requirements evolve.&nbsp;</em></li>\n<li><em>A desktop or laptop computer is required to complete the application and onboarding process. Mobile devices are not supported.</em></li>\n"}],"salaryRange":{"min":25,"max":25,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-hour-wage"},"text":"Maps Personalization Quality Reviewer - Japanese (Japan)","country":"JP","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<div>We&rsquo;re seeking an experienced Quality Reviewer to audit work completed by raters evaluating a personalization feature within a maps/search experience.</div>\n<div>As a Reviewer, you will ensure outputs meet formatting and guideline requirements, are logically aligned to scenarios, and include complete, accurate evidence.&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Contract type:</strong> Freelance</div>\n<div><strong>Language:</strong> Japanese (Japan)</div>\n<div><strong>Estimated volume: </strong><span data-teams=\"true\">Approximately 30 hours per week, depending on the required review target and project volume.</span>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</div>\n</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>What you will do:</strong></div>\n<div>\n<ul>\n<li>Review rater worksheets for compliance with formatting requirements.<!----></li>\n<li><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!---->Verify that responses are logically correct and aligned with the assigned scenarios.<!----></li>\n<li><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!---->Assess ratings and rationales for accuracy, consistency, and completeness.<!----></li>\n<li><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!---->Confirm that required screenshots, retrievals, and personalization evidence meet project guidelines.<!----></li>\n<li><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!---->Provide clear, concise, and actionable feedback; request corrections where needed.<!----></li>\n<li><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!---->Flag ambiguous cases, systemic issues, or guideline gaps to the project team.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"We’re seeking an experienced Quality Reviewer to audit work completed by raters evaluating a personalization feature within a maps/search experience.\nAs a Reviewer, you will ensure outputs meet formatting and guideline requirements, are logically aligned to scenarios, and include complete, accurate evidence. \n \nContract type: Freelance\nLanguage: Japanese (Japan)\nEstimated volume: Approximately 30 hours per week, depending on the required review target and project volume. \nStart date: ASAP\n \nWhat you will do:\nReview rater worksheets for compliance with formatting requirements.\nVerify that responses are logically correct and aligned with the assigned scenarios.\nAssess ratings and rationales for accuracy, consistency, and completeness.\nConfirm that required screenshots, retrievals, and personalization evidence meet project guidelines.\nProvide clear, concise, and actionable feedback; request corrections where needed.\nFlag ambiguous cases, systemic issues, or guideline gaps to the project team.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/weloglobal/2e0cf51e-414f-409d-95e0-526c7079e26e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/weloglobal/2e0cf51e-414f-409d-95e0-526c7079e26e/apply"}